  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programme for Country Partnership (PCP) for Albania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To build on the achievements of the Country Programme in Albania (2020#2024), the Government of Albania has officially requested the transition to the Programme for Country Partnership (PCP). The PCP will serve as a platform for delivering coordinated, high-impact interventions that promote inclusive and sustainable industrial development in line with Albania#s national priorities. UNIDO and the Government of Albania will work closely to ensure the effective mobilization of resources and foster partnerships with national institutions, development partners and the private sector, supporting the successful implementation of projects and delivering tangible results on the ground. Drawing on UNIDO#s expertise and access to global best practices in sustainable industrial development, the PCP will scale up support to help Albania advance in areas such as the circular economy, quality infrastructure, industrial policymaking, economic diversification and the greening and modernization of value chains. Through its programmatic and multi-stakeholder approach, the PCP will promote innovative, inclusive and sustainable business models while fostering long-term development impact through resilient and durable solutions, in line with the #leaving no one behind# approach.</narrative>
  </description>
